   "id": "march",
   "title": "The army splits on the march",
   "time": "June to 22 August 1071",
   "narrative": "Romanos marched his composite army across Anatolia, resting at Sebasteia and reaching Theodosiopolis in June. Believing Alp Arslan was far off, he turned towards Lake Van to retake Manzikert and the fortress of Khliat. Near the end he divided his force: Joseph Tarchaniotes took part of the regulars, the Varangians and the Pecheneg and Frankish mercenaries towards Khliat, while the emperor went on to Manzikert. What became of Tarchaniotes is unclear, but he never rejoined the field army, which was left far smaller than planned.",
