   "id": "foragers",
   "title": "Foragers meet the Seljuk army",
   "time": "24 August",
   "narrative": "Foraging parties under Nikephoros Bryennios ran into the main Seljuk force and fell back on Manzikert. Romanos doubted it was the Sultan's whole army and sent the Armenian general Basilakes with cavalry; they were routed and Basilakes was captured. The emperor then drew up his men and sent Bryennios' left wing out, and it was nearly surrounded by the fast Turkish horsemen before it withdrew. At night the Seljuks vanished into the hills, leaving no target for a counter-attack.",
